d-response discriminator rather than assuming heartbeat rejection is not contact.\"\n    },\n    \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"consumption\",\n    \"counterevidence\": [\n      \"LeaderLeaseTimeout explicitly promises step-down without quorum contact, not on every rejected reply.\",\n      \"Source describes lease as heartbeat-connectivity checking rather than a read-only query lease.\",\n      \"Ordinary, snapshot and pipeline reply paths check higher terms before refreshing contact.\",\n      \"Pending VerifyLeader can step down on a negative heartbeat response.\",\n      \"TestRaft_LeaderLeaseExpire checks disconnected-peer role loss within two lease intervals; it does not specifically exercise delayed pipeline completion.\",\n      \"CommitTimeout drives ordinary/pipeline traffic even without client writes; after pipeline Success=false the implementation falls back to ordinary replication.\",\n      \"Ordinary in-memory AppendEntries propagates timeout errors and does not refresh contact on that branch.\"\n    ],\n    \"unknowns\": [\n      \"Requirement gap narrowed: AppendFuture.Response explicitly requires Error completion and success; the lease contract concerns actual contact, but an API mismatch alone is not a completed authority-loss finding.\",\n      \"Local execution gap: run a real in-memory pipeline timeout, correlate its request/future identity, observe Error and marker before/after actual pipelineDecode consumption.\",\n      \"Initial-prefix and same-history gaps: full cluster election, pipeline activation and isolated no-contact interval have not been executed. Remote processing without reply remains possible.\",\n      \"Endpoint gap: whether this refresh changes a scheduled lease decision or public leadership-loss timing remains unobserved; fallback replication and negative verification remain protective alternatives.\"\n    ],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"trigger_rationale\": \"Reading the previously deferred pipeline producer revealed that 